{
  "story": {
    "text": "Amy, a young student who loves watercolor painting, was working in her dormitory on a half-finished painting of campus trees. Her paintbrush, watercolor box, and drawing board were on the narrow desk, and she meant to finish the painting that evening. Lisa came to the doorway wearing sports clothes and said, \"Amy, I am about to do sports activities. Do you want to come with me?\" Amy stared at the drawing board, hesitated because she still wanted to paint, but finally put down the brush and went with Lisa so she would not seem unfriendly. While Amy was away, Lisa later returned first, put her bulky sports bag on the chair in front of Amy's desk, and did not notice that it blocked the drawing board from the doorway. After the sports activities, Amy and Lisa returned to the dorm; Amy was holding a water bottle in one hand and a damp towel in the other, Lisa cheerfully said, \"That was fun; I thought you were done painting for today,\" and now Amy stands by the door, unable to see her drawing board behind Lisa's bag, and must decide what to do next."
  }
}

